; PaperVeil – D01 network-boundary sandbox profile (offline variant).
;
; Used by scripts/network-check.sh, case (a): a PaperVeil processing run
; WITHOUT the LLM must succeed with ALL networking denied, proving that
; local processing and storage work completely offline (docs/ZIELZUSTAND.md
; D01: "Ohne konfigurierte Upload-Verbindung funktioniert lokale Verarbeitung
; und Speicherung offline").
;
; Everything else stays allowed (file access, process spawning, OCR, …);
; only networking of any kind is denied – no DNS, no sockets, no loopback,
; no telemetry, no fallback of any sort.
;
; NOTE: `sandbox-exec` is deprecated by Apple but still present on macOS 27.2
; (/usr/bin/sandbox-exec). scripts/network-check.sh checks for its existence
; and falls back to connection sampling only if it is ever removed.
;
; The loopback-only companion profile used for the WITH-LLM run (case b) is
; generated by scripts/network-check.sh because it embeds the LM Studio port:
;   (version 1)
;   (allow default)
;   (allow network-outbound (remote ip "localhost:1234"))
;   (deny network*)
; On macOS 27 the SBPL ip filter accepts only `*` or `localhost` as the host
; part, so "127.0.0.1:1234" is not writable there; "localhost:1234" matches the
; loopback connection. See docs/acceptance/network-and-logs.md.

(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network*)
